('Escape velocity from Earth''s surface is approximately', '$11.2\;\text{km/s}$', '$7.9\;\text{km/s}$', '$3.2\;\text{km/s}$', '$22.4\;\text{km/s}$', 'option1', '$v_e = \sqrt{2gR} = \sqrt{2 \times 9.8 \times 6.4 \times 10^6} \approx 11.2\;\text{km/s}$.', 'p_satellites_escape', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Orbital velocity of a satellite near Earth''s surface is approximately', '$3.1\;\text{km/s}$', '$11.2\;\text{km/s}$', '$7.9\;\text{km/s}$', '$15.8\;\text{km/s}$', 'option3', '$v_o = \sqrt{gR} = \sqrt{9.8 \times 6.4 \times 10^6} \approx 7.9\;\text{km/s}$.', 'p_satellites_escape', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The relation between escape velocity $v_e$ and orbital velocity $v_o$ near the surface is', '$v_e = \sqrt{2}\;v_o$', '$v_e = 2v_o$', '$v_e = v_o$', '$v_e = v_o/\sqrt{2}$', 'option1', '$v_e = \sqrt{2gR}$ and $v_o = \sqrt{gR}$. So $v_e = \sqrt{2}\;v_o$.', 'p_satellites_escape', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
