-- ============================================================
('Pressure at depth $h$ in a fluid of density $\rho$ is', '$\rho g/h$', '$\rho g h$', '$\rho h/g$', '$g h/\rho$', 'option2', 'Gauge pressure at depth $h$: $P = \rho g h$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Pascal''s law states that', 'Pressure depends on the shape of the container', 'Pressure increases with depth', 'Fluids are incompressible', 'Pressure applied to a confined fluid is transmitted equally in all directions', 'option4', 'Pascal''s law: pressure applied to a confined fluid is transmitted undiminished throughout.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The SI unit of pressure is', 'Pascal ($\text{Pa}$)', 'Newton ($\text{N}$)', 'Joule ($\text{J}$)', 'Dyne', 'option1', '$1\;\text{Pa} = 1\;\text{N/m}^2$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Atmospheric pressure is approximately', '$9.8 \times 10^4\;\text{Pa}$', '$1.013 \times 10^3\;\text{Pa}$', '$1.013 \times 10^5\;\text{Pa}$', '$1.013 \times 10^6\;\text{Pa}$', 'option3', 'Standard atmospheric pressure $= 1.013 \times 10^5\;\text{Pa} = 1\;\text{atm}$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A hydraulic press works on the principle of', 'Bernoulli''s principle', 'Archimedes'' principle', 'Pascal''s law', 'Newton''s third law', 'option3', 'A hydraulic press uses Pascal''s law: pressure is transmitted equally, allowing force multiplication.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Pressure at a point in a fluid at rest is', 'Same in all directions', 'Greater in the downward direction', 'Greater in the horizontal direction', 'Zero', 'option1', 'At a point in a static fluid, pressure is isotropic (same in all directions).', 'p_fluid_pressure', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Archimedes'' principle states that the buoyant force equals', 'Weight of fluid displaced', 'Weight of the body', 'Volume of the body', 'Density of the fluid', 'option1', 'Buoyant force $= \rho_{fluid} \times V_{displaced} \times g =$ weight of fluid displaced.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Pressure at the bottom of a $10\;\text{m}$ water column is ($\rho = 1000\;\text{kg/m}^3$, $g = 10\;\text{m/s}^2$)', '$10^4\;\text{Pa}$', '$10^5\;\text{Pa}$', '$10^3\;\text{Pa}$', '$10^6\;\text{Pa}$', 'option2', '$P = \rho g h = 1000 \times 10 \times 10 = 10^5\;\text{Pa}$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A hydraulic lift has pistons of area $10\;\text{cm}^2$ and $100\;\text{cm}^2$. A force of $50\;\text{N}$ on the small piston lifts', '$5000\;\text{N}$', '$50\;\text{N}$', '$5\;\text{N}$', '$500\;\text{N}$', 'option4', '$F_2 = F_1 \times A_2/A_1 = 50 \times 100/10 = 500\;\text{N}$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A body of density $\rho_b$ floats in a fluid of density $\rho_f$. Fraction submerged is', '$\rho_b/\rho_f$', '$\rho_f/\rho_b$', '$1 - \rho_b/\rho_f$', '$\rho_b \rho_f$', 'option1', 'At equilibrium: $\rho_b V g = \rho_f V_{sub} g$. Fraction $= V_{sub}/V = \rho_b/\rho_f$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('An ice cube floats in water. When it melts, the water level', 'Falls', 'Rises', 'Remains the same', 'First rises then falls', 'option3', 'Ice displaces its own weight of water. When it melts, it produces exactly that volume of water. Level stays same.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A U-tube manometer has water ($\rho = 1000\;\text{kg/m}^3$) and oil. If oil column is $20\;\text{cm}$ and water column is $16\;\text{cm}$, oil density is', '$800\;\text{kg/m}^3$', '$1000\;\text{kg/m}^3$', '$1250\;\text{kg/m}^3$', '$600\;\text{kg/m}^3$', 'option1', '$\rho_{oil} \times 20 = 1000 \times 16$. $\rho_{oil} = 16000/20 = 800\;\text{kg/m}^3$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A block of wood ($\rho = 600\;\text{kg/m}^3$) floats in water. The fraction above water is', '$2/5$', '$3/5$', '$1/2$', '$1/3$', 'option1', 'Fraction submerged $= 600/1000 = 3/5$. Fraction above $= 1 - 3/5 = 2/5$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The absolute pressure at depth $h$ in a liquid is', '$\rho g h$', '$P_0 + \rho g h$', '$P_0 - \rho g h$', '$P_0 \rho g h$', 'option2', 'Absolute pressure $=$ atmospheric pressure $+$ gauge pressure $= P_0 + \rho g h$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A solid sphere of density $\rho_s$ and radius $r$ is submerged in liquid of density $\rho_l$. Apparent weight is', '$\frac{4}{3}\pi r^3 \rho_l g$', '$\frac{4}{3}\pi r^3 \rho_s g$', '$\frac{4}{3}\pi r^3(\rho_s - \rho_l)g$', '$\frac{4}{3}\pi r^3(\rho_s + \rho_l)g$', 'option3', 'Apparent weight $= W - F_b = \frac{4}{3}\pi r^3 g(\rho_s - \rho_l)$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A body weighs $50\;\text{N}$ in air and $40\;\text{N}$ in water. Its density is ($\rho_w = 1000\;\text{kg/m}^3$)', '$5000\;\text{kg/m}^3$', '$4000\;\text{kg/m}^3$', '$1250\;\text{kg/m}^3$', '$2500\;\text{kg/m}^3$', 'option1', 'Buoyant force $= 10\;\text{N}$. Volume $= 10/(1000 \times 10) = 10^{-3}\;\text{m}^3$. Mass $= 50/10 = 5\;\text{kg}$. Density $= 5/10^{-3} = 5000\;\text{kg/m}^3$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A balloon of volume $V$ and mass $m$ is filled with gas of density $\rho_g$ in air of density $\rho_a$. For it to rise, the condition is', '$\rho_g > \rho_a$', '$\rho_g V > m$', '$m > \rho_a V$', '$\rho_a V > m + \rho_g V$', 'option4', 'Buoyant force $> $ total weight: $\rho_a V g > (m + \rho_g V)g$. So $\rho_a V > m + \rho_g V$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A container has two immiscible liquids of densities $\rho_1$ and $\rho_2$ ($\rho_1 < \rho_2$) with heights $h_1$ and $h_2$. Pressure at the bottom is', '$P_0 + \rho_1 g h_1 + \rho_2 g h_2$', '$P_0 + (\rho_1 + \rho_2)g(h_1 + h_2)$', '$P_0 + \rho_2 g(h_1 + h_2)$', '$P_0 + \rho_1 g h_2 + \rho_2 g h_1$', 'option1', 'Pressure adds layer by layer: $P = P_0 + \rho_1 g h_1 + \rho_2 g h_2$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A cube of side $a$ and density $\rho_c$ floats at the interface of two liquids ($\rho_1 < \rho_c < \rho_2$). Fraction in the lower liquid is', '$\rho_c/\rho_2$', '$(\rho_c - \rho_1)/(\rho_2 - \rho_1)$', '$(\rho_2 - \rho_c)/(\rho_2 - \rho_1)$', '$\rho_1/\rho_c$', 'option2', 'Let fraction $x$ in lower liquid. $\rho_c a^3 g = \rho_2 x a^3 g + \rho_1(1-x)a^3 g$. $\rho_c = \rho_2 x + \rho_1 - \rho_1 x$. $x = (\rho_c - \rho_1)/(\rho_2 - \rho_1)$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A cylindrical vessel of area $A$ has a hole of area $a$ at depth $h$. Speed of efflux is (Torricelli''s theorem)', '$\sqrt{2gh}$', '$\sqrt{gh}$', '$2gh$', '$\sqrt{gh/2}$', 'option1', 'Torricelli''s theorem: $v = \sqrt{2gh}$ (speed of efflux from a hole at depth $h$).', 'p_fluid_pressure', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A tank of height $H$ has a hole at height $h$ from the bottom. The range of the liquid jet on the ground is maximum when $h$ equals', '$H/2$', '$H/4$', '$H/3$', '$3H/4$', 'option1', 'Range $= 2\sqrt{h(H-h)}$. Maximum when $h(H-h)$ is max, i.e., $h = H/2$.', 'p_fluid_pressure', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),

