-- p_superposition_standing (7 easy, 7 medium, 7 hard = 21)
-- ============================================================
('The principle of superposition states that when two waves overlap, the resultant displacement is', 'The algebraic sum of individual displacements', 'The product of individual displacements', 'The average of individual displacements', 'Zero', 'option1', 'Superposition principle: $y = y_1 + y_2$. The net displacement is the algebraic sum of individual wave displacements.', 'p_superposition_standing', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Standing waves are formed by the superposition of', 'Two waves in the same direction', 'Two waves of different frequencies', 'A single wave', 'Two identical waves travelling in opposite directions', 'option4', 'Standing (stationary) waves result from superposition of two waves of same frequency and amplitude travelling in opposite directions.', 'p_superposition_standing', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In a standing wave, points of zero displacement are called', 'Crests', 'Antinodes', 'Nodes', 'Troughs', 'option3', 'Nodes are points of permanently zero displacement in a standing wave.', 'p_superposition_standing', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In a standing wave, points of maximum displacement are called', 'Antinodes', 'Nodes', 'Crests', 'Compressions', 'option1', 'Antinodes are points of maximum displacement in a standing wave.', 'p_superposition_standing', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The distance between two consecutive nodes in a standing wave is', '$\lambda/2$', '$\lambda$', '$\lambda/4$', '$2\lambda$', 'option1', 'Consecutive nodes are separated by half a wavelength: $\lambda/2$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Beats are produced when two waves of', 'Very different frequencies superpose', 'Same frequency superpose', 'Slightly different frequencies superpose', 'Same amplitude superpose', 'option3', 'Beats occur when two waves of nearly equal frequencies interfere, producing periodic variation in loudness.', 'p_superposition_standing', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Beat frequency equals', 'The average of the two frequencies', 'The sum of the two frequencies', 'The difference of the two frequencies', 'The product of the two frequencies', 'option3', 'Beat frequency $f_{beat} = |f_1 - f_2|$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The fundamental frequency of a string fixed at both ends of length $L$ is', '$2v/L$', '$v/L$', '$v/(4L)$', '$v/(2L)$', 'option4', 'Fundamental mode: $\lambda_1 = 2L$. $f_1 = v/\lambda_1 = v/(2L)$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The harmonics present in a string fixed at both ends are', 'Only odd harmonics', 'All harmonics ($f, 2f, 3f, ...$)', 'Only even harmonics', 'Only the fundamental', 'option2', 'A string fixed at both ends supports all harmonics: $f_n = nv/(2L)$ for $n = 1, 2, 3, ...$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('An open organ pipe of length $L$ has fundamental frequency', '$v/L$', '$v/(4L)$', '$v/(2L)$', '$2v/L$', 'option3', 'Open pipe: antinodes at both ends. $\lambda_1 = 2L$. $f_1 = v/(2L)$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A closed organ pipe of length $L$ has fundamental frequency', '$v/(2L)$', '$v/(4L)$', '$v/L$', '$v/(3L)$', 'option2', 'Closed pipe: node at closed end, antinode at open end. $\lambda_1 = 4L$. $f_1 = v/(4L)$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The harmonics present in a closed organ pipe are', 'Only even harmonics', 'All harmonics', 'Only odd harmonics ($f, 3f, 5f, ...$)', 'Only the fundamental', 'option3', 'Closed pipe supports only odd harmonics: $f_n = nv/(4L)$ for $n = 1, 3, 5, ...$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Two tuning forks of frequencies $256\;\text{Hz}$ and $260\;\text{Hz}$ are sounded together. Beat frequency is', '$8\;\text{Hz}$', '$516\;\text{Hz}$', '$2\;\text{Hz}$', '$4\;\text{Hz}$', 'option4', '$f_{beat} = |260 - 256| = 4\;\text{Hz}$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('When a wave reflects from a rigid boundary, it undergoes a phase change of', '$\pi$ (180°)', '$0$', '$\pi/2$', '$2\pi$', 'option1', 'Reflection from a rigid (fixed) boundary causes a phase reversal of $\pi$ radians.', 'p_superposition_standing', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A string fixed at both ends vibrates in its third harmonic. The number of nodes and antinodes are', '$3$ nodes and $4$ antinodes', '$4$ nodes and $3$ antinodes', '$3$ nodes and $3$ antinodes', '$4$ nodes and $4$ antinodes', 'option2', 'The $n$th harmonic has $n+1$ nodes and $n$ antinodes. Third harmonic: $4$ nodes, $3$ antinodes.', 'p_superposition_standing', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A closed pipe and an open pipe have the same fundamental frequency. The ratio of their lengths is', '$2:1$', '$1:2$', '$1:1$', '$1:4$', 'option2', 'Closed: $f = v/(4L_c)$. Open: $f = v/(2L_o)$. Equal: $v/(4L_c) = v/(2L_o)$. $L_c/L_o = 1/2$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A string of length $1\;\text{m}$ fixed at both ends vibrates at $500\;\text{Hz}$ in its fundamental mode. The speed of the wave is', '$2000\;\text{m/s}$', '$500\;\text{m/s}$', '$250\;\text{m/s}$', '$1000\;\text{m/s}$', 'option4', '$f_1 = v/(2L)$. $v = 2Lf_1 = 2 \times 1 \times 500 = 1000\;\text{m/s}$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The first overtone of a closed pipe has frequency', '$f_1$', '$2f_1$', '$4f_1$', '$3f_1$ (where $f_1$ is fundamental)', 'option4', 'Closed pipe: only odd harmonics. First overtone $= 3f_1$ (third harmonic).', 'p_superposition_standing', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A tuning fork of unknown frequency produces $5$ beats/s with a fork of $512\;\text{Hz}$ and $3$ beats/s with a fork of $514\;\text{Hz}$. The unknown frequency is', '$517\;\text{Hz}$', '$507\;\text{Hz}$', '$509\;\text{Hz}$', '$511\;\text{Hz}$', 'option1', 'With $512$: $|f - 512| = 5$, so $f = 507$ or $517$. With $514$: $|f - 514| = 3$, so $f = 511$ or $517$. Common value: $f = 517\;\text{Hz}$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('An open pipe of length $L$ resonates at its second harmonic. The wavelength of the sound wave is', '$L$', '$2L$', '$L/2$', '$4L$', 'option1', 'Open pipe second harmonic: $\lambda_2 = 2L/2 = L$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A sonometer wire of length $1\;\text{m}$ under tension $T$ vibrates at $256\;\text{Hz}$. To get $512\;\text{Hz}$ with the same wire, the tension should be', '$T/2$', '$2T$', '$4T$', '$T/4$', 'option3', '$f = (1/2L)\sqrt{T/\mu}$. $f \propto \sqrt{T}$. For $f'' = 2f$: $T'' = 4T$.', 'p_superposition_standing', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved');